[size=5][b]Build Advisor[/b][/size]
[i]The strongest build for your character, starred in the game's own menus: character creation, Withers' respec and every level-up.[/i]

Build Advisor shows a strong community build (Patch 8 meta) for your character and marks the right choices while you make them, in:
[list]
[*][b]New game character creation[/b] (Tav, Dark Urge and origin characters)
[*][b]Withers respec[/b] (the respec screen, then every level-up that follows)
[*][b]Every level-up[/b]
[*][b]Party view[/b] (press the hotkey any time to see the next level-up for the selected character)
[/list]

[size=4][b]How it shows the build[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]In the game menus:[/b] every choice the build wants on the current screen gets a star: race, subrace, class, subclass, background, deity, skills and expertise, feats and their own choices, spells and cantrips, spells to prepare, the spell to replace, fighting styles, manoeuvres, invocations, metamagic and more. Tiles and spell icons also get a rainbow outline. Point-buy rows and Ability Improvement rows show the target score, e.g. "Strength (17, +2)".
[*][b]Advisor window (F7):[/b] the build, a "DO THIS NOW" list for the current level, [OK] / [CHANGE] checks for your race, class and point-buy, and the full level 1-12 plan.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Builds included[/b][/size]
22 builds, among them Sorcadin, Oathbreaker Paladin, Lockadin, Path of Giants Barbarian, Throwzerker, Tavern Brawler Monk, Battle Master Fighter, Gloom Stalker multiclasses, Light Domain Cleric, Evocation Wizard, Storm Sorcerer, Sorlock and Moon / Stars Druid. Each origin character has a suggested build; you can pick any build for any character in the window (remembered per character).

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Baldur's Gate 3 (Patch 8).
[*][url=https://github.com/Norbyte/bg3se]BG3 Script Extender[/url] v20 or newer. It is a separate project and is not included; [url=https://github.com/LaughingLeader/BG3ModManager]BG3 Mod Manager[/url] installs it in one click.
[*]Game language English for the in-menu marks (the advisor window works in any language).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install Script Extender (BG3 Mod Manager: [i]Tools > Download and Extract the Script Extender[/i]).
[*]Drag [b]BuildAdvisor.pak[/b] into BG3 Mod Manager (or [i]File > Import Mod[/i]).
[*]Move Build Advisor to the active mods, then [i]Save Load Order[/i] and [i]Export Load Order to Game[/i].
[*]Start the game. The window opens on its own in character creation and level-up; [b]F7[/b] toggles it.
[/list]
The download also holds [b]INSTALL.md[/b] and the offline [b]Handbook.html[/b] (the marks in the menus, the advisor window, all builds, settings, FAQ).

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
In the window: build picker, [i]Show all builds[/i], [i]Highlight in game menus[/i], [i]Auto-open[/i]. Script Extender console: !ba_toggle, !ba_dump, !ba_hotkey F7.

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Disable or remove Build Advisor in the mod manager. Nothing is written to your saves.

[size=4][b]Works with Loot Advisor[/b][/size]
Installed together with [url=https://github.com/md12ol/LootAdvisor]Loot Advisor[/url], the items Loot Advisor recommends follow the build you picked here. Each mod also works on its own.

[size=4][b]Source and bug reports[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/md12ol/BuildAdvisor]github.com/md12ol/BuildAdvisor[/url] (MIT licence). The pak contains outline textures recoloured from the game's own frame textures, under Larian's modding terms; the mod is free.
